# Test [[.Name]]

Discover existing test entry points from nearby project guidance, package scripts
and CI. Reuse the prepared tools, fixtures and working commands. Keep assertions
in the project's test framework; a new runner is not required.

Choose focused checks that cover the affected behaviour. Reconsider that selection
when the changed component changes: a previous component's passing tests do not
validate the new repair. Use focused checks while iterating and the relevant native
suite when ready. Preserve the task's scope rather than claiming unrun gates passed.

Component feedback and aggregate quality gates can have different scopes. Use the
project's supported focused invocation while retaining full-suite coverage and
other repository gates. Verify each chosen command passes on repaired code; a
passing full suite does not make a permanently failing focused command usable.

For regressions, establish that the relevant test fails before the fix and passes
afterwards. Reuse existing assertions and fixtures where they express the contract.
Keep lengthy diagnostics in a local log and inspect relevant excerpts when useful;
label omissions instead of treating truncated output as complete evidence.
